{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knots.KauffmanTL3","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knots.KauffmanTL3","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":81,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.torus819_knot_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.torus819_knot_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":520,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L520-L523","doc":"**`8₁₉` is a nontrivial knot** (machine-proved, AXIOM-FREE): its Jones\npolynomial `δ·V(8₁₉)` differs from the unknot's `δ`, because `V(8₁₉) ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.torus819_jones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.torus819_jones","kind":"theorem","line":509,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L509-L517","doc":"**The link library reproduces the known `8₁₉` Jones polynomial**\n(machine-proved, AXIOM-FREE): `jones (8₁₉ closure) = δ · V(8₁₉)` with\n`V(8₁₉) = -A⁻³² + A⁻²⁰ + A⁻¹²` (the closed-form `(3,4)` torus-knot Jones\npolynomial). The widest exact identity in the ladder (Jones span 20, an\n8-crossing knot) and a third chiral cross-check, after the trefoil (brick 4).\nThe `δ` is the 1-component normalisation; `jones (8₁₉) / δ = V(8₁₉)`. (Two\nvalue lemmas + transitivity, as in `figure_eight_jones`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.jones_torus819_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.jones_torus819_value","kind":"theorem","line":502,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L502-L507","doc":"The bracket reduction of the `8₁₉` closure (a length-8 3-braid — the heaviest\nkernel-`decide` reduction in the ladder, ~70 s):\n`jones (8₁₉) = A⁻³⁴ + A⁻³⁰ - A⁻²² - A⁻¹⁸ - A⁻¹⁴ - A⁻¹⁰`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.delta_mul_jonesTorus819","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.delta_mul_jonesTorus819","kind":"theorem","line":496,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L496-L499","doc":"`δ · V(8₁₉)` fully reduced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.jonesTorus819Reduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.jonesTorus819Reduced","kind":"def","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L486-L490","doc":"`δ · V(8₁₉)` fully bracket-reduced — the Jones polynomial of the `(σ₁σ₂)⁴`\nclosure: `A⁻³⁴ + A⁻³⁰ - A⁻²² - A⁻¹⁸ - A⁻¹⁴ - A⁻¹⁰`. Shared by\n`delta_mul_jonesTorus819` and `jones_torus819_value` (avoids duplicating the literal). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.jonesTorus819","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.jonesTorus819","kind":"def","line":478,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L478-L484","doc":"The `8₁₉` Jones polynomial `V(8₁₉) = -A⁻³² + A⁻²⁰ + A⁻¹²` in the Kauffman\n`A`-variable (`t = A⁻⁴`: `-t⁸ + t⁵ + t³`). This is the closed-form torus-knot\nJones polynomial `V(T(m,n)) = t^{(m-1)(n-1)/2}(1 - t^{m+1} - t^{n+1} + t^{m+n})\n/ (1 - t²)` at `(m,n) = (3,4)`, which reduces to `t³(1 + t² - t⁵)`. `8₁₉` is\nchiral; the all-positive `(σ₁σ₂)⁴` selects this handedness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.torus819","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.torus819","kind":"def","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L473-L476","doc":"The torus knot `8₁₉ = T(3,4)`, as the closure of the all-positive 3-braid\n`(σ₁σ₂)⁴` (underlying permutation a 3-cycle ⇒ a single component, a knot). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.hopf_link_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.hopf_link_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":457,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L457-L461","doc":"**The Hopf link is nontrivial** (machine-proved, AXIOM-FREE): the `σ₁²` closure\n(`Hopf ⊔ unknot`) has Jones polynomial differing from the 3-component unlink's\n`δ³`, so the Hopf sublink is genuinely linked (a nonzero linking number, here\nvisible as `V(Hopf) ≠ δ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.hopf_link_jones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.hopf_link_jones","kind":"theorem","line":443,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L443-L455","doc":"**The link library reproduces the known Hopf-link Jones polynomial**\n(machine-proved, AXIOM-FREE): `jones (σ₁² closure) = δ² · V(Hopf)` with\n`V(Hopf) = -A⁻² - A⁻¹⁰`. The **first named multi-component link** validated\nagainst a literature invariant — bricks 1–2 only proved the Borromean bracket\n*differed* from the unlink's (a `≠`), never reproduced a *known* `V` (an `=`).\nOf the two `δ` factors, one is the split unknot forced by the third strand\n(`Hopf ⊔ unknot`), one the 1-component normalisation; the residue\n`jones (hopf) / δ² = V(Hopf)` is the genuine 2-component Hopf-link Jones\npolynomial. This exercises the library on the framework's CAL-3 / `m_π`\nobject (`Vol(Hopf) = 0`). (Two value lemmas + transitivity, as in\n`figure_eight_jones`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.jones_hopf_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.jones_hopf_value","kind":"theorem","line":437,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L437-L441","doc":"The bracket reduction of the Hopf (`⊔ unknot`) closure:\n`jones (hopf) = -A⁻¹⁴ - 2A⁻¹⁰ - 2A⁻⁶ - 2A⁻² - A²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.delta_sq_mul_jonesHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.delta_sq_mul_jonesHopf","kind":"theorem","line":431,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L431-L435","doc":"`δ² · V(Hopf)` fully reduced. The two `δ` factors are the split unknot of the\n3-braid closure (`Hopf ⊔ unknot`) and the 1-component normalisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.jonesHopfReduced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.jonesHopfReduced","kind":"def","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L422-L425","doc":"`δ² · V(Hopf)` fully bracket-reduced — the Jones polynomial of the `σ₁²`\nclosure (`Hopf ⊔ unknot`): `-A⁻¹⁴ - 2A⁻¹⁰ - 2A⁻⁶ - 2A⁻² - A²`. Shared by\n`delta_sq_mul_jonesHopf` and `jones_hopf_value` (avoids duplicating the literal). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.jonesHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.jonesHopf","kind":"def","line":417,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L417-L420","doc":"The Hopf-link Jones polynomial `V(Hopf) = -A⁻² - A⁻¹⁰` in the Kauffman\n`A`-variable (`t = A⁻⁴`: `-t^{1/2} - t^{5/2}`). The Hopf link is chiral; the\nall-positive `σ₁²` selects this handedness (the mirror Hopf has `-A² - A¹⁰`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.hopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.hopf","kind":"def","line":412,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L412-L415","doc":"The Hopf link, as the closure of `σ₁²` in `B₃`. With `σ₂` unused the third\nstrand is disjoint, so the closure is `Hopf ⊔ split-unknot` (3 components).\nThe framework's CAL-3 / `m_π` object (`Vol(Hopf) = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.trefoil_knot_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.trefoil_knot_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L387-L391","doc":"**The trefoil is a nontrivial knot** (machine-proved, AXIOM-FREE): its Jones\npolynomial `δ·V(3₁)` differs from the unknot's `δ` (the closure of the 3-cycle\nbraid `σ₁σ₂`), because `V(3₁) ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.trefoil_jones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.trefoil_jones","kind":"theorem","line":375,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L375-L385","doc":"**The link library reproduces the known trefoil Jones polynomial**\n(machine-proved, AXIOM-FREE): `jones (3₁ closure) = δ · V(3₁)` with\n`V(3₁) = -A⁻¹⁶ + A⁻¹² + A⁻⁴` (classically `-t⁴ + t³ + t`). A second exact\npolynomial identity against a literature invariant — now for a *chiral* knot,\ncomplementing the amphichiral figure-eight (brick 3) and the Borromean link\n(bricks 1–2). The `δ` is the 1-component normalisation (`jones (unknot) = δ`);\nthe reduced invariant `jones (3₁) / δ = V(3₁)`. (Proved by transitivity through\nthe two value lemmas, as in `figure_eight_jones`: a single `decide` on the\ncombined `jones`+`δ·V` reduction exceeds the elaboration heartbeat budget.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.jones_trefoil_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.jones_trefoil_value","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L369-L373","doc":"The bracket reduction of the trefoil closure: `jones (3₁) = A⁻¹⁸ - A⁻¹⁰ - A⁻⁶ - A⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.delta_mul_jonesTrefoil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.delta_mul_jonesTrefoil","kind":"theorem","line":361,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L361-L366","doc":"`δ · V(3₁)` in fully reduced form, `A⁻¹⁸ - A⁻¹⁰ - A⁻⁶ - A⁻²` (small-`LP`\narithmetic). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.jonesTrefoil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.jonesTrefoil","kind":"def","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L350-L355","doc":"The trefoil Jones polynomial `V(3₁) = -A⁻¹⁶ + A⁻¹² + A⁻⁴` in the Kauffman\n`A`-variable (the substitution `t = A⁻⁴` gives the classical `-t⁴ + t³ + t`).\nThis is the chirality the all-positive braid `(σ₁σ₂)²` selects in this\nconvention; the mirror trefoil has `-t⁻⁴ + t⁻³ + t⁻¹`. The asymmetry\n`V(3₁) ≠ V(mirror)` is the Jones polynomial detecting trefoil handedness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.trefoil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.trefoil","kind":"def","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L345-L348","doc":"The trefoil knot `3₁`, as the closure of the all-positive 3-braid `(σ₁σ₂)²`\n— the `(3,2)` torus knot (its underlying permutation is a 3-cycle, so the\nclosure is a single component, a knot). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.figure_eight_knot_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.figure_eight_knot_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L326-L330","doc":"**The figure-eight is a nontrivial knot** (machine-proved, AXIOM-FREE): its\nJones polynomial `δ·V(4₁)` differs from the unknot's `δ` (the closure of the\n3-cycle braid `σ₁σ₂`), because `V(4₁) ≠ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.figure_eight_jones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.figure_eight_jones","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L312-L324","doc":"**The link library reproduces the known figure-eight Jones polynomial**\n(machine-proved, AXIOM-FREE): `jones (4₁ closure) = δ · V(4₁)` with\n`V(4₁) = A⁸ - A⁴ + 1 - A⁻⁴ + A⁻⁸`. An *exact polynomial identity* against a\nliterature invariant — a stronger validation of the Kauffman/`TL₃` bracket\nthan brick 1's Borromean nontriviality (which only compared two brackets for\ninequality). The `δ` is the 1-component normalisation (`jones (unknot) = δ`);\nthe reduced invariant `jones (4₁) / δ = V(4₁)`. Since `4₁` is the\nq₀-calibration knot (`m_μ/m_e = Vol(4₁)/ℏ_q²`), this exercises the library on a\nframework-central knot. (Proved by transitivity through the two value lemmas:\na single `decide` on the combined `jones`+`δ·V` reduction exceeds even a\n1 M-heartbeat elaboration budget, so the two reductions are kept separate.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.jones_figureEight_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.jones_figureEight_value","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L306-L310","doc":"The bracket reduction of the figure-eight closure: `jones (4₁) = -A¹⁰ - A⁻¹⁰`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.delta_mul_jonesFigureEight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.delta_mul_jonesFigureEight","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L299-L303","doc":"`δ · V(4₁)` in fully reduced form, `-A¹⁰ - A⁻¹⁰` (small-`LP` arithmetic). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.jonesFigureEight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.jonesFigureEight","kind":"def","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L290-L293","doc":"The figure-eight Jones polynomial `V(4₁) = A⁸ - A⁴ + 1 - A⁻⁴ + A⁻⁸`\n(Kauffman `A`-variable; the substitution `t = A⁻⁴` recovers the classical\n`t⁻² - t⁻¹ + 1 - t + t²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.figureEight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.figureEight","kind":"def","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L285-L288","doc":"The figure-eight knot `4₁`, as the closure of the 3-braid `(σ₁σ₂⁻¹)²` (its\nunderlying permutation is a 3-cycle, so the closure is a single component —\na knot). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.borromean_crossing_minimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.borromean_crossing_minimal","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L249-L271","doc":"**Crossing-minimality of the Borromean confinement operator** (machine-\nchecked by `native_decide`; axioms `Lean.ofReduceBool` + `Lean.trustCompiler`,\ni.e. trusting the Lean compiler — cross-checked against the Python enumeration\noracle, both yielding minimal crossing number `= 6`). Among 3-braid closures\n(the framework's 3-quark setting):\n\n1. the Borromean braid `(σ₁σ₂⁻¹)³` is pure, Brunnian and nontrivial (a valid\n   confined 3-quark state), and has word-length `6`;\n2. **no** braid word of length `< 6` is simultaneously Brunnian and\n   nontrivial.\n\nHence `6` is the minimal braid crossing number of a nontrivial Brunnian\n3-braid, achieved by the Borromean rings — closing the last residual of\n[`prop:confinement-operator-selection`](../../../quantum-observable-universe/particle-interactions/confinement-operator-selection.md)'s\ntopological selection. Scope: 3-braid closures and braid-word crossing number\n(the framework's setting), not full link-theoretic uniqueness; nontriviality\nis the Jones invariant — a sufficient, not complete, certificate, which only\nstrengthens the lower bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.wordsBelow6","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.wordsBelow6","kind":"def","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L245-L246","doc":"Every braid word of length `< 6` (lengths `0..5`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.allWords","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.allWords","kind":"def","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L239-L243","doc":"All `4ⁿ` braid words of length `n` over `{σ₁^±, σ₂^±}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.nontrivialBrunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.nontrivialBrunnian","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L235-L237","doc":"A pure, Brunnian, nontrivial 3-braid closure — a confined 3-quark candidate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.linkNontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.linkNontrivial","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L231-L233","doc":"Nontrivial: the Jones polynomial differs from the 3-unlink's `δ³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.jones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.jones","kind":"def","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L227-L229","doc":"The writhe-normalised Kauffman bracket — the **Jones invariant** of the\nclosure, an ambient-isotopy invariant (value `δ³` on any trivial 3-link). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.writheUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.writheUnit","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L222-L225","doc":"The R1-normalising monomial `(-A³)^(-writhe) = (-1)^w · A^(-3w)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.writhe","kind":"def","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L218-L220","doc":"Writhe (signed crossing count) of a braid word = its exponent sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.brunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.brunnian","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L213-L216","doc":"Brunnian (decidable core): deleting any one strand leaves the unlink, i.e.\nevery 2-sublink has exponent sum `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.b2class","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.b2class","kind":"def","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L199-L211","doc":"`B₂ ≅ ℤ` exponent sum of the 2-braid left after deleting strand `k`\n(crossings touching strand `k` are dropped; the braid still permutes\npositions). `= 0` iff that 2-sublink closes to the unlink. Mirrors\n`confinement_operator_selection.lean`'s `b2class` in `{σ₁,σ₂}` indexing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.isPure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.isPure","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L196-L197","doc":"Pure: the closure has exactly 3 components. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.perm","kind":"def","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L188-L194","doc":"Underlying strand permutation of a 3-braid word (each position holds a\nstrand; `σ₁` swaps positions 0,1; `σ₂` swaps positions 1,2). The closure has\n3 components (is *pure*) iff this is the identity `(0,1,2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.borromean_link_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.borromean_link_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L146-L152","doc":"**The Borromean rings are a nontrivial link** (machine-proved, axiom-free):\nthe Kauffman bracket of `(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³`'s closure differs from the 3-unlink's.\nBoth closures have writhe `0`, so the unnormalised bracket separates them.\nThis is the link-nontriviality invariant the crossing-minimality proof needs\n(where the `B₂ ≅ ℤ` exponent-sum test of sublink triviality does not reach,\n`B₃` being non-abelian). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.unlink3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.unlink3","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L142-L143","doc":"The trivial 3-braid (closes to the 3-component unlink). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.borromean","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L139-L140","doc":"The Borromean braid `(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)³` (generators 1-indexed here as `σ₁,σ₂`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.bracket","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L132-L137","doc":"Kauffman bracket of the braid's plat/trace closure. Loop counts of the\nclosed `TL₃` basis diagrams: `1 ↦ δ³`, `e₁,e₂ ↦ δ²`, `e₁e₂,e₂e₁ ↦ δ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.d3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.d3","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L130-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.d2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.d2","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L129-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.evalWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.evalWord","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L125-L127","doc":"A 3-braid word as a list of `(generator ∈ {1,2}, positive?)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.sig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.sig","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L118-L123","doc":"Kauffman image of a braid generator: `σᵢ ↦ A·1 + A⁻¹·eᵢ`, inverse\n`σᵢ⁻¹ ↦ A⁻¹·1 + A·eᵢ` (`i ∈ {1,2}`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.mul","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L113-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.bmul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.bmul","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L104-L111","doc":"Product of two `TL₃` basis elements (index, scalar `1` or `δ`), from the\nrelations `eᵢ² = δ eᵢ`, `e₁e₂e₁ = e₁`, `e₂e₁e₂ = e₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.oneTL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.oneTL","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L102-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.zeroTL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.zeroTL","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.addAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.addAt","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L94-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.get","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.get","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L91-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.TL.delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.TL.delta","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L88-L89","doc":"The loop value `δ = -A² - A⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.instReprTL.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.instReprTL.repr","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knots.instReprTL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knots.instReprTL","kind":"instance","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knots/KauffmanTL3.lean#